# ouroboros#183: sqrt and exp are ELEMENTWISE over a list on the VM. The
# emitter intercepted them by name and emitted the C intrinsic without
# checking the argument, so a list argument died at build time with the
# internal "emit_num on non-numeric node list". The intrinsic now applies
# only to a provably numeric argument; anything else takes the builtin
# call. Controls: numeric arguments at module scope and through a
# parameter still take the intrinsic (4, 1). A list reaching a numeric
# parameter (`f of ys`) is the mixed-evidence class (#135/#148), not this.
xs is [1, 4, 9]
r is sqrt of [xs]
print of r
e is exp of [[0, 0]]
print of e
print of (sqrt of 16)
define f(v) as:
    return sqrt of v
print of (f of 1)
